description: Always prefer Bun runtime and Bun APIs over Node
alwaysApply: true
---

# Bun Runtime Preferred

- Use Bun as the default runtime for scripts, tooling, and server execution.
- Prefer Bun-native APIs and libraries when an equivalent exists.
- Do not introduce new direct dependencies on Node-specific runtime APIs unless explicitly required.
- Prefer `bun` commands over `node`, `npm`, `npx`, and `pnpm` in examples and instructions.
- When reading/writing files, hashing, or serving HTTP, check Bun built-ins first before adding Node-based packages.
- If Node compatibility is unavoidable, add a short comment explaining why Bun-native alternatives are insufficient.
